  "steps": [
    "Saved animation clips list duplicate literal names, source intervals and complete UUIDs in author order. Any string parameter can explicitly insert an ID; numeric parameters have no helper. Reading or selecting alone does not dirty the form or revoke an approved review.",
    "At 390px Chinese/English/Japanese preserve the focused text node, selection range, tentative clip and approved review without horizontal overflow. Explicit insertion revokes approval. Binding switches preserve each row and incomplete numeric text; Cancel leaves draft and files unchanged.",
    "A directory failure preserves values and the approved ordinary edit. Retry succeeds without changing that review, and Cancel still preserves the source.",
    "legacy saved directory gives an explicit message and preserves approved ordinary edits.",
    "no-clips saved directory gives an explicit message and preserves approved ordinary edits.",
    "no-animation saved directory gives an explicit message and preserves approved ordinary edits.",
    "While reading, ordinary controls remain usable. A response arriving after a binding switch never fills a row; a response from a closed dialog cannot populate a reopened session.",
    "Apply updates only the unsaved ordinary draft, which can reopen and reload the directory. Ordinary Save writes the exact reviewed BOM/CRLF text; only the behavior JSON changes, all other author files remain identical, and reopening retains the ID."
  ],
